---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import AttachmentDemo from '../../components/AttachmentDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs
  title="Attachment"
  description="File cards, chips, and type icons for uploads and file references, with upload states, retry, remove, a carousel group, and a local drop zone."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Attachment</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    Shows a file a person attached, uploaded, or referenced. Use
    <code>FileAttachment</code> for a ready-made row, card, mention, or chip, and the <code>Attachment</code> parts when
    you need your own layout.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <AttachmentDemo client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">File attachments</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Staged uploads in a composer"
      code={`import { AttachmentGroup, FileAttachment } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/attachment";

<AttachmentGroup variant="carousel" aria-label="Attached files">
  {uploads.map((item) => (
    <FileAttachment
      key={item.id}
      variant="chip"
      file={{
        id: item.id,
        name: item.file.name,
        mediaType: item.file.type,
        size: "48 KB",
        state: item.kind, // "ready" | "uploading" | "processing" | "error"
        source: { kind: "local", file: item.file },
      }}
      preview
      viewable
      onRemove={() => remove(item.id)}
      onRetry={() => retry(item)}
    />
  ))}
</AttachmentGroup>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>variant</code> picks the shape:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>"list"</code> (default): a row with icon, name, and status line.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>"grid"</code>: a card with a large preview above the name.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>"inline"</code>: a compact pill for text.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>"chip"</code>: a 36px chip for composers and messages.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The status line shows <code>file.size</code> when ready, which can also be a short source such as “Google Drive”
      or “Saved in Files”. Busy files show a spinner, and <code>"error"</code> shows “Upload failed” with a Retry button
      when you pass <code>onRetry</code>. <code>onRemove</code>
      adds a remove button. Images with a <code>url</code> show a thumbnail.
    </p>
    <p>
      Opening: <code>viewable</code> opens the file in the full-screen
      <code>FileViewer</code> on click, with syntax colors for code and text. Pass
      <code>onOpen</code> instead to open it your own way, such as a canvas or a download; it is disabled while the file
      is busy. With neither, the name is plain text.
      <code>actionLabel="Download"</code>
      names the button “Download …” instead of “Inspect …”.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>preview</code> peeks at the file in a card after hovering or focusing the name for 400ms: the image, or the
      first 24 lines of text, code, JSON, or Markdown. Other formats and failed uploads get no card. Both props need{' '}
      <code>file.source</code> or <code>file.url</code>. Wrap the app in <code>FileRenderersProvider</code> to view
      sheets, Office files, and formatted Markdown.
    </p>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="References in a sent message"
      code={`<FileAttachment
  variant="chip"
  file={{ id, name: "Supplier price sheet", mediaType, size: "Google Drive", state: "ready" }}
  onOpen={openInCanvas}
/>

<FileAttachment
  variant="chip"
  file={{ id, name: "Loading file…", mediaType: "", size: "", state: "processing" }}
  onOpen={() => undefined}
/>

<FileAttachment
  variant="chip"
  actionLabel="Download"
  file={{ id, name: "Price comparison.xlsx", mediaType, size: "52 KB", state: saving ? "processing" : "ready" }}
  onOpen={save}
/>`}
    />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Groups</h2>
    <p>
      <code>AttachmentGroup</code> lays out attachments. <code>"carousel"</code>
      (default) scrolls one row sideways with fading edge arrows;
      <code>"grid"</code> makes two columns, three from 640px;
      <code>"inline"</code> wraps; <code>"list"</code> stacks. Give a carousel an
      <code>aria-label</code>. Viewable attachments in a group share one viewer that steps through them in page order
      with Previous, Next, and the arrow keys. Closing it returns focus to the last file shown.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Parts</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Build your own attachment"
      code={`<Attachment state="uploading" size="sm" orientation="horizontal">
  <AttachmentTrigger aria-label="Open Q3 launch deck.pptx" onClick={open} />
  <AttachmentMedia>
    <FileTypeIcon name="Q3 launch deck.pptx" mediaType={type} />
  </AttachmentMedia>
  <AttachmentContent>
    <AttachmentTitle>Q3 launch deck.pptx</AttachmentTitle>
    <AttachmentDescription>Uploading 1.2 MB of 2.8 MB</AttachmentDescription>
  </AttachmentContent>
  <AttachmentActions>
    <AttachmentAction aria-label="Remove Q3 launch deck.pptx" onClick={remove}>
      <X />
    </AttachmentAction>
  </AttachmentActions>
</Attachment>`}
    />
    <ul>
      <li>
        <code>state</code>: <code>"idle"</code> dashes the border,
        <code>"uploading"</code> and <code>"processing"</code> shimmer the title,
        <code>"error"</code> turns it red, <code>"done"</code> (default) is plain.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>size</code>: <code>"lg"</code> (40px media, the default),
        <code>"md"</code> (32px), <code>"sm"</code> (28px).
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>orientation</code>: <code>"horizontal"</code> (default) or
        <code>"vertical"</code>, which stacks the media above the text and floats actions over its corner.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>AttachmentMedia variant="image"</code> crops an
        <code>img</code>; the default <code>"icon"</code> centers an icon or spinner.
      </li>
      <li>
        <code>AttachmentTrigger</code> stretches over the card so a click anywhere opens it. It accepts{' '}
        <code>render</code> for a link.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">File type icons</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Rows, mentions, and dialog headings"
      code={`<FileTypeIcon name="Returns policy.pdf" mediaType="application/pdf" />
<FileTypeIcon name="Price list 2026.xlsx" mediaType={type} size="lg" />`}
    />
    <p>
      A decorative paper glyph with the extension in a colored badge: red for PDF, green for sheets, blue for documents
      and Google files, orange for slides, light blue for images, and gray for everything else. <code>"sm"</code>{' '}
      (default) is 20 × 24px; <code>"lg"</code> is 30 × 36px. A name without an extension shows no badge.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Local files</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Drop zone with in-memory files"
      code={`<AttachmentDropzone accept=".txt,.md,.pdf,.docx" disabled={busy} onFiles={add} />
{files.map((file, index) => (
  <LocalFileAttachment key={index} file={file} preview viewable onRemove={() => remove(index)} />
))}`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>AttachmentDropzone</code> takes drops or a “Choose files” button and hands the files to <code>onFiles</code>
      . It uploads nothing.
      <code>accept</code> defaults to documents, sheets, slides, PDF, text, JSON, Google shortcuts, images, and common
      source files.
      <code>LocalFileAttachment</code> shows a <code>File</code> as a chip with a live image thumbnail, and passes{' '}
      <code>preview</code> and
      <code>viewable</code> through.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Each open button is named “Inspect name” or “Download name”; remove and retry buttons are named “Remove name” and
      “Retry name”. Busy chips have a spinner named “Uploading…” or “Processing…”. File type icons are hidden from
      assistive tech because the name is always beside them.
    </p>
    <p>
      The carousel is a labelled region. Each item is a group, focus scrolls it into view, and Left and Right scroll it
      when focus is inside. The edge arrows are for pointers, so Tab never lands on a button that vanishes at the end of
      the row. The drop zone's button opens the system file picker. Transitions take 120 to 180ms; with reduced motion
      the title shimmer and smooth scrolling stop.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Cards use <code>--sprout-surface</code>, <code>--sprout-line</code>,<code>--sprout-hover</code>, and{' '}
      <code>--sprout-danger</code>. File type icons use <code>--sprout-file-paper</code>,<code>--sprout-file-edge</code>
      , <code>--sprout-file-label</code>, and one badge color per kind: <code>--sprout-file-generic</code>,
      <code>-pdf</code>, <code>-sheet</code>, <code>-document</code>,<code>-slides</code>, and <code>-image</code>. Each
      has a light and a dark value.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
